      "notes": "York County is Maine's southernmost county and its most densely populated outside the Portland area, with seasonal coastal communities driving heavy property-lookup demand. The data comes from the same Maine GeoLibrary statewide organized-towns service used by Cumberland County. Layer 10 (FeatureServer/10) carries polygon geometry with COUNTY, TOWN, PROP_LOC, MAP_BK_LOT, and STATE_ID. Layer 9 (FeatureServer/9) is the assessor attribute table -- no geometry -- carrying OWNER1/OWNER2 and mailing address fields; join to layer 10 on MAP_BK_LOT. Filter to York County with COUNTY='YORK'; municipalities include Biddeford, Saco, Sanford, Kennebunk, York, Kittery, Wells, and Berwick. Important caveat: GeoLibrary submissions are voluntary and asynchronous -- some towns update quarterly, others lag by a year or more. For current ownership or assessment, check the individual town assessor's office or the Maine Revenue Services PAS database. Unorganized territories in York County use a separate MEGIS service."
